# Intent: The stop word ends a ringing timer or alarm (patches 091 to 093, 049). The stop-word callback first asks maipai_timers_request_dismiss and, when a ring was going, ends it and does nothing else; otherwise it aborts speech as before. The timer code arms the stop word when a ring starts and disarms it when the ring ends (hal_bridge::stop_word_arm, best effort: it needs the model and some free internal RAM; a disarm never disarms it while the unit is speaking). UNVERIFIED on the unit: patch 049 armed it only while speaking, so whether the model hears "stop" in the standby state is the first thing to test.
# Placement: unit (the ring and the audio path run on the robot)
# Upstream: main/application.cc of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT)
# Check after a flash: ring a timer and say "stop" from a metre away: the ring ends and the log says "Stop word heard while a timer rings"; if it does not, check the log for "Stop word not armed" (low internal RAM); the touch always works.
diff --git a/firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.cc b/firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.cc
